.ly_state/session/audit_reports/role20_p10_gate_tuning_compliance_audit_20260610.md:16:- Scope: Compliance audit of P10 gate tuning after Role21 approval for `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py`, `scripts/run_phase35_backtest.py`, `tests/phase35/test_p10_multi_horizon_blend.py`, and supplied L2/L3 reports.
.ly_state/session/audit_reports/role20_p10_gate_tuning_compliance_audit_20260610.md:20:### P1 - JSON/fold reporting can persist the wrong horizon metadata after partial horizon success
.ly_state/session/audit_reports/role20_p10_gate_tuning_compliance_audit_20260610.md:24:- `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1652-1695` stores `horizon_details` for both included and excluded horizons, in requested-horizon insertion order.
.ly_state/session/audit_reports/role20_p10_gate_tuning_compliance_audit_20260610.md:25:- `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1702-1724` only falls back to T+5 baseline when no horizons survive or when blend quality is non-positive. A partial-success case can continue on the normal multi-horizon path.
.ly_state/session/audit_reports/role20_p10_gate_tuning_compliance_audit_20260610.md:26:- `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1755-1762` says it uses the first successful horizon, but actually uses `first_horizon = list(horizon_details.keys())[0]`. That is the first requested horizon, which can be excluded.
.ly_state/session/audit_reports/role20_p10_gate_tuning_compliance_audit_20260610.md:27:- `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:2118-2137` writes that selected `gate_metadata`, `gate_results`, and `gated_alphas` into `FoldMetrics`.
.ly_state/session/audit_reports/role20_p10_gate_tuning_compliance_audit_20260610.md:28:- `scripts/run_phase35_backtest.py:60-73` and `scripts/run_phase35_backtest.py:376` persist the `FoldMetrics.gate_metadata` and aliases into JSON.
.ly_state/session/audit_reports/role20_p10_gate_tuning_compliance_audit_20260610.md:32:If horizon 1 is excluded but horizon 3 or 5 is included and the blend succeeds, JSON can report `selection_source: excluded`, `used_fallback_candidates: false`, empty `gated_alphas`, and gate counts from the excluded horizon while the actual signal came from a later included horizon. If the included later horizon used relaxed fallback candidates, that fallback label is not reliably persisted. This violates focus item 2 and item 6: fallback candidates must be labeled and persisted, and JSON/reporting must be truthful.
.ly_state/session/audit_reports/role20_p10_gate_tuning_compliance_audit_20260610.md:36:Persist metadata from the included horizon(s), not the first requested horizon. Minimum acceptable fix: select the first horizon where `included == True`. Better fix: persist per-horizon diagnostics for all requested horizons, including included/excluded status, gate metadata, quality metrics, and blend weight.
.ly_state/session/audit_reports/role20_p10_gate_tuning_compliance_audit_20260610.md:40:- `tests/phase35/test_p10_multi_horizon_blend.py:303-321` covers partial horizon success only at `_blend_horizon_signals()` level.
.ly_state/session/audit_reports/role20_p10_gate_tuning_compliance_audit_20260610.md:41:- Existing serialization tests at `tests/phase35/test_p10_multi_horizon_blend.py:1243-1311` verify a supplied metadata object is serialized, but do not verify `run_fold()` chooses truthful metadata in partial-success scenarios.
.ly_state/session/audit_reports/role20_p10_gate_tuning_compliance_audit_20260610.md:45:1. Relaxed gate explicit opt-in only; strict defaults unchanged: PASS
.ly_state/session/audit_reports/role20_p10_gate_tuning_compliance_audit_20260610.md:46:   - Engine defaults are strict at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:188-194`.
.ly_state/session/audit_reports/role20_p10_gate_tuning_compliance_audit_20260610.md:47:   - CLI defaults are strict at `scripts/run_phase35_backtest.py:167-182`.
.ly_state/session/audit_reports/role20_p10_gate_tuning_compliance_audit_20260610.md:50:2. FAIL strings are not counted as pass; fallback candidates labeled and persisted: FAIL
.ly_state/session/audit_reports/role20_p10_gate_tuning_compliance_audit_20260610.md:51:   - FAIL string counting is fixed by `_is_gate_verdict_pass()` at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:37-93` and robust gate counts at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1294-1297`.
.ly_state/session/audit_reports/role20_p10_gate_tuning_compliance_audit_20260610.md:53:   - Persistence is not truthful in partial-success folds because `run_fold()` can copy metadata from an excluded first requested horizon.
